## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
The release workflow previously only reacted to tag refs, so merged pull requests and direct pushes to main were not handled correctly.

### Decisions Made
- Trigger on pushes to main so both PR merges and direct pushes are covered.
- Scan every commit introduced by the push so a tag on a merged commit is found.
- Preserve the existing vMAJOR.MINOR and vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH validation.

### Trade-offs
A squash merge does not retain the original PR commit object in main history; the release tag must point to the resulting squash commit in that case.
